From a4246e36820a205e854adc9c3bf48e5aae6f2d92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:37:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] CP7 5,000 targets, phase D (prototype): read a staged run
 by target range
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pages (one per staged analysis chunk, each <= 8,000,000 bytes, sha256-bound to
the run's document and semantic hashes) plus a header, written after the
segments; the page index is written last so a failed or half-paged job cannot
be read. Readers erp_cp7_read_analysis_pages_v1 / _page_v1 (authenticated,
SECURITY DEFINER, owner cp7_capture, same access-epoch and actor checks as the
segment reader); refuse_paged guard (CP7_ANALYSIS_RUN_PAGED) for whole reads.
Prototype SQL stays under tests (not installed).

Proof f05-staged-pages (2 tests): over the staged parity corpus with pages of
1, 3 and 7 targets, header + pages reproduce the analysis, its text and the
Original byte for byte (191 runs, 1,982 pages, 1,812 page edges, 80/80 single
builds identical); readers' refusals, privileges and immutability.

Frontend: strict page-set/header/page parser (sizes, hashes, run binding, range
continuity, totals, item membership) and a staged view that shows whole-run
totals from the server, then "Target 501–1.000 dari 5.000" pages; reports,
reminders and AI are stated unavailable for staged runs. Single runs unchanged.
Measurement scripts for Original composition and result storage.

